{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114787","id":3159487704,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc68UfTY","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114787","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114787.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114787.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114787","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114787/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114787/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114787/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/cf2b59f874e30738cc1a9925a407d1e397aabaed","number":114787,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Make `RichTextLabel`'s `text` represent the tag stack ","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolves: \r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114639\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105026\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100168\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/94630\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/79420\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/61260\r\n\r\nAlso Resolves:\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100772\r\n\r\nImplements:\r\n* https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/8739\r\n\r\nGodot's RichTextLabels parse and convert BBCode Text into a TagStack / ItemTree. Since Godot 4.0 (?), rendering / logic is primarily driven by this Tag Stack / Item Tree; the Text Property exists mostly for inspector convenience, and the occasional hard overwrite via code. This frequently leads to confusion when scripts modify a Label via Add_text and the such, but the changes are not reflected in the Text property. See the 6 open Duplicate Issue reports linked above, and the numerous notes about the text property being out of sync in the RichTextLabel documentation.\r\n\r\nThis PR seeks to address this issue by having the RichTextLabel update the Text Property as the ItemTree is modified to keep the two in sync. I accomplish this by:\r\n* Adding utility functions to the Item Classes that output appropriate BBCode tags, hopefully making the BBCode <-> ItemTree conversions 2-way\r\n* Having RichTextLabel store a Sync_text, representing all of the TagStack generated by `push_*() & pop()` calls. Whenever a user interacts with the Text property, they are actually interacting with the concatenation of text + sync_text.\r\n* User-generated BBCode is never over-written, duplicated, or regenerated. The `internal_stack_editing` flag makes it clear when the items being added are not directly from user-written text.\r\n\r\nI have verified most simple behaviors produce correct BBCode - I may have missed some edge cases, but in the current build, every time I read the Text property it contained exactly the full BBCode I expected, and if I pasted the output back into another RichTextLabel node, they displayed identically. \r\n\r\nExisting Behaviors Changed:\r\n* The Text property and the Tag Stack are functionally identical from a user perspective. There should be no way to modify one or the other that doesn't sync them together.\r\n* Fixed a minor issue where RTL.push_bold() then RTL.append_text(\"[i]bi\") would not correctly create a BoldItalics node in the tree.\r\n* All other logic should remain the same, and similarly performant. No extra tree traversals are performed\r\n\r\nExtremely open to feedback - is this the right approach? Is it performant enough? Are there edge cases that keeping Sync_Text does not account for? Should this be pursued at all? ","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_ur